%% Tauri plugins — full flow
%% Pure Mermaid. No Markdown fence.

flowchart TD
    trigger([A native capability is needed]) --> own{Is this the app's own logic,<br/>or a platform capability?}

    own -->|own logic| command[Write a plain #tauri::command —<br/>simpler, no permission plumbing]
    own -->|platform capability| pick{Which plugin?}

    pick -->|Settings / small KV| store[Store]
    pick -->|Relational data| sql[SQL]
    pick -->|Secrets or credentials| strong[Stronghold — NEVER Store]
    pick -->|Open a file or URL| opener[Opener — not Shell]
    pick -->|Run a program| shell[Shell]
    pick -->|Something else| cat[Check the catalogue]

    store --> support
    sql --> support
    strong --> support
    opener --> support
    shell --> support
    cat --> support

    support{Does the target platform<br/>support this plugin?}
    support -->|desktop-only, app also ships mobile| degrade[Design the feature to DEGRADE<br/>on mobile — dialogs, shell, tray,<br/>global shortcuts are desktop-only]
    support -->|yes| wire
    degrade --> wire

    wire[Wire it in THREE places:<br/>1. Rust crate  2. JS package<br/>3. capability permission]

    wire --> third{Is the capability permission added?}
    third -->|no| runtimefail[It compiles and then FAILS AT RUNTIME<br/>with a permission error. Add it.]
    third -->|yes| scope
    runtimefail --> third

    scope{Is this fs or shell?}
    scope -->|fs| fsscope[Scope allow paths to what the app owns —<br/>unscoped fs:default is read access<br/>to the user's whole disk]
    scope -->|shell| shscope[Allowlist SPECIFIC commands with fixed<br/>arguments — never let the frontend<br/>choose the binary]
    scope -->|neither| verify
    fsscope --> verify
    shscope --> verify

    command --> verify

    verify{Call succeeds at runtime?<br/>Permission is the narrowest that works?}
    verify -->|denied| third
    verify -->|too broad| scope
    verify -->|good| done([Done: wired, scoped, least-privilege])

    classDef gate fill:#fff4e6,stroke:#d97706,color:#7c2d12
    classDef terminal fill:#ecfdf5,stroke:#059669,color:#064e3b
    class own,pick,support,third,scope,verify gate
    class trigger,done terminal
